  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5). 
Agesilao treated with his ally Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Agesilao treated with his ally Circe (#8).
  In spring, Agesilao prepared his armies to defend Mare Frigidis and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Ships bearing the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
cruised into the Sea province of the Arrak Sea, a land garrisoned by the 
forces of Agesilao.  The Arrak Sea was conquered by Lakes (#64)'s fleet.  
Lakes leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 1 Whales, 1 Fleet and 1 Mermen.
  With the advent of the early summer season Agesilao was tutored in White 
Magic by Nixie.  Agesilao practiced his White Magic and his skill in White 
Magic went up.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer came.  Agesilao marched on the 
Argyre Sea (#1707) with his forces.
  In fall, Agesilao practiced his White Magic diligently for many weeks, but 
could make no significant progress.

  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) into the Forest province of Katmai, 
ruled by Agesilao.  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Katmai without any major 
battles.  Alain leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 3 Dragons and 1 
Trolls.
  Agesilao gained the Holy Sword.  Nixie returned to Valhalla, having tried 
his best to execute his assignments.

  The fall cooled into early winter.  Stonebrick was resurrected by the 
spell cast by Agesilao.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Agesilao for this year.


  Agesilao Treated with Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, but Babba Sissoko 
did not react to his amicable overtures.  It is hoped that next year, both 
Kings will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Agesilao treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Agesilao treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  
Agesilao treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Agesilao treated with his 
ally Kahn (#6).  Agesilao treated with his ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  
Agesilao treated with his ally Circe (#8).

  Here is the financial report for Agesilao's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 51 gold in revenue.  7 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 98th Eagles trained well and improved in quality.  50 gold was 
expended to maintain our armies.  Agesilao was left with 21 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tancred
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I boldly marched my command into the First Sea (#1809).
  With the coming of the early summer season I enlisted the 98th Eagles in 
the First Sea to serve me.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  I transferred the 
245th Phalanx to the provincial Eagle chieftain in the First Sea.
  During fall, I flew over to Mare Ritalis.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I attempted an illegal move.  
I could not move to the Christmas Sea because armies can't move overland and 
use transport in the same turn.  Instead, I worked hard on my Tactics but 
was frustrated in my self-improvement efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Tancred


From: Negumba
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I marched on the Sahuagin Sea (#1706) with my command.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I marched my forces into the 
Argyre Sea (#1707).  I marched along an unconventional route through the 
Argyre Sea and raised our exploration there to 100%.
  In late summer, I prepared my armies to defend Mare Frigidis and the 
surrounding provinces.
  With the coming of the fall season I prepared my armies to defend Mare 
Frigidis and the surrounding provinces.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I tried to improve my White 
Magic, but the task seemed beyond my natural ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Negumba


From: Nixie
To: Agesilao

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I cast a Bless spell.  Mare Frigidis was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Mare Frigidis.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  I practiced my White Magic 
diligently for months, but could make no headway.
  In late summer, I investigated the Loch, meaning to root out its dark 
secrets.  I encountered the Mermaid.  Casting a Telekinetic Storm spell, I 
directed scintillating, interlacing strands of magic, which proved useless 
in the underwater environs of the Loch.  Chanting her silver words of magic 
into a great Charm spell, the Mermaid gestured with her hands but the spell 
seemed ineffective against me.  I chanted my mysterious words of magic and 
cast a Psychic Blast spell, projecting psychic waves of stunning force 
towards the Mermaid.  In her pathetic stunned state, the Mermaid could not 
decide what to do about her predicament.

  I moved to bow range.  The Mermaid could do nothing in her stunned state.  
I shot a hard arrow at the Mermaid and scored on the Mermaid, inflicting 1 
points of damage.  The Mermaid shook her head and recovered from her stunned 
condition.

  I darted into melee range.  The Mermaid maneuvered to a good defensive 
position.  Then the Mermaid lunged at me with all her strength and scored on 
me, doing 3 points of damage.  I circled left and violently attacked 
the Mermaid and scorched the Mermaid with 7 damage points.  The Mermaid sank 
down, mortally injured.  I looked down with satisfaction at the remains of 
the Mermaid.  I swam over to a mound of treasure and bagged the Holy Sword.  
I examined the Holy Sword and discovered the following properties:
  The Holy Sword has a +20% chance to hit and does +3 damage against normal 
opponents, and +40%/+5 against undead creatures.  In addition, the sword 
confers the protection of the gods upon its wielder.  This protection 
operates automatically in all encounters.  The effect is the same as a Holy 
Symbol spell cast at skill level 4, except it causes no damage.
  I looted 1 gold from the treasure trove of the Mermaid.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Loch.  In my travels, I saw 
no monster.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  I gathered my courage and cautiously 
entered the Catacombs.  I drew out my Holy Sword.  I encountered the Troll.  
Weaving my silver words of magic into a great Telekinetic Storm spell, I 
gestured with my hands and scored 9 damage points on the Troll.  Some 
fragments flew towards me and damaged me, inflicting 3 damage points.  My 
efforts raised my prowess in Psychic Magic.
  The Troll moved to bow range.  Casting a Psychic Blast spell, I directed 
glowing, interlacing strands of magic, projecting psychic waves of stunning 
force towards the Troll.  Stunned, the Troll could only shake its head in 
bewilderment.
  I took careful aim and fired an arrow at the Troll and inflicted 4 damage 
points.  In its pathetic stunned state, the Troll could not determine what 
to do.
  I charged into the melee.  The Troll stood stunned, unable to regain its 
senses.  I circled right and attacked the Troll and scored on the Troll, 
doing 6 points of damage.  Stunned, the Troll could only shake its head in 
bewilderment.  I fled unceremoniously from the dangerous scene.
  While scouting the Catacombs, I saw a Roulette Wheel which seemed to be of 
a magical nature.  While adventuring, I saw no marauding monsters.
  Agesilao gained the Holy Sword.  I returned to Valhalla, having tried my 
best to execute my assignments.


  Thy humble servant,   Nixie


